"""Write human-adjudicated batch-10 reports from inspect_fold.py artifacts."""
import csv,json,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
NOTES={
'H091':('REFUTED','The apparent s15 deficit at 1727.26 is embedded in a large positive post-gap excursion: the two local flanks differ by 20.2 ppt. Well-covered predicted windows in s14, s40, s41 and s60 are flat to about 0.2 ppt, and s75 is only 0.4 ppt. The selected 28.418 d eclipse fold is thus produced by a discontinuous excursion rather than repeated box-shaped eclipses.','A genuine unrelated eclipse elsewhere on this star is outside this selected-fold conclusion.'),
'H092':('REFUTED','The s18 window is at a sector level transition; the s58 2.1 ppt local median is on the decay of a much larger bright excursion (left/right baselines differ by 4.0 ppt). The fully sampled s85 predicted window is a 1.5 ppt brightening relative to its sides. These opposite, slope-contaminated occasions refute the selected 31.857 d repeating dip.','A pixel comparison could identify the origin of the sector transitions if the variability itself is pursued.'),
'H093':('REFUTED','The well-covered s35 predicted core is 0.3 ppt brighter than its local sides. S61 sits on a broad rising trend and s99 on the recovery from a gap/level change; their 2.4 and 2.0 ppt local medians are not repeated isolated eclipses. The P2 result reuses the same s99 feature.','Investigate broad variability with an independent aperture if it becomes a separate target of interest.'),
'H094':('PLAUSIBLE','Two shallow local depressions coincide with P-screened windows: 1.4 ppt in s33 and 1.4 ppt in s87. S33 is also about 1.2 ppt in KSPSAP, an alternative extraction of the same photons. The s6 core has only six cadences and no right baseline after a gap, so it is not a sensitive null. A newly fetched sector-108 3x3 TESScut aperture has 52 core and 129/130 flank samples around the exact P-screening prediction at 4316.47026 and is flat (-0.02 ppt), but the individual flank MAD is about 1.2 ppt and time-correlated noise is not calibrated; this challenges rather than decisively excludes a 1.4 ppt event. WCS places the target at pixel (2.79, 2.26), inside that aperture, whose median total flux is 6815 e/s. Sector 107 is 0.54 ppt amid a slope; sector 98 has only about 7 e/s in the central 3x3 despite WCS placement and is unusable as a target measurement. The weak earlier profiles could be genuine dips at another integer alias or be variability. Their centers, source and cycle count remain insecure.','Localize the s33/s87 depressions, measure their centers and test integer aliases against newer coverage before assigning an orbital period.'),
'H095':('REFUTED','The only well-sampled P occasion in s82 lies on a broad drop with a 5.3 ppt difference between left and right local baselines; the core itself is only 0.1 ppt below the combined sides. S55 is near the sector endpoint with no right baseline. The fold minimum is a slope/coverage mixture, not a repeated eclipse.','A different period search would be needed to assess unrelated variability.'),
'H096':('REFUTED','The s90 predicted depression is on a multi-day fading tail and local sides differ by about 10.2 ppt. S63 and s64 have densely sampled, nearly flat predicted cores (about 0.1 ppt). S99 and s100 predictions fall in coverage gaps. The selected 28.532 d fold is driven by the s90 trend rather than a recurrent eclipse.','Pixel or independent aperture data could characterize the long s90 excursion, which is separate from the rejected fold.'),
'H097':('REFUTED','The 3.9 ppt s74 predicted core is in a dramatic post-gap recovery: the full sector rises by tens of ppt. The s80 predicted core is fully sampled and flat; s26/s40 have one-sided coverage. The narrow folded minimum is an alignment of the s74 recovery, not evidence for repeated eclipses.','Characterize the sector-edge recovery separately if scientifically useful.'),
'H098':('REFUTED','The s88 predicted core overlaps a broad positive excursion and strong local slope (7.3 ppt left/right mismatch); s90 has a densely covered flat core. Several other predicted windows intersect sector edges or gaps. The selected 43.913 d fold does not have repeatable eclipse morphology.','A fresh search could test whether any unrelated isolated dip in the long time series warrants follow-up.'),
'H099':('REFUTED','The s60 1.4 ppt local deficit falls in the relaxation from a large sector-opening bright excursion; its flanks differ by 3.3 ppt, so its contribution to the fold is a positive trend artifact. The s20 predicted core is near 0.1 ppt, while s47 is about 0.4 ppt, comparable to the weak screened depth but embedded in broad modulation rather than a clear local box. These data reject the selected stacked eclipse shape; s47 alone is too weak and insecure to establish an isolated event.','Inspect s47 with independent pixel photometry if its weak depression is pursued.'),
'H100':('PLAUSIBLE','A distinct s86 dip near BTJD 3640.16 reaches about 6.8 ppt against local flanks and survives in DET and SYS_RM columns. SAP_X shifts by roughly 0.025 pixel over the dip, exactly returning at egress; this may indicate an aperture response or an off-target eclipsing source. A crude s86 TESScut difference is dominated by spatially broad background change and does not localize the deficit. The well-covered s58 predicted core is flat, contradicting an exact 35.052 d recurrence, while s19 has only three core cadences and lacks a left baseline. Current sector-footprint follow-up found s59 ends at BTJD 2936.690, 2.43 d before its screened prediction, and s85 ends at 3636.048, 4.11 d before the s86 prediction; neither supplies another expected occasion. A real isolated event remains possible; the fold period is not a measured eclipse period.','Localize the s86 deficit with background-controlled difference pixels and capable neighbors, then seek another observing occasion and test integer-cycle aliases.'),
}
rows=[];hashes=[]
for row in csv.DictReader((B/'queue.csv').open(newline='')):
 sid=row['sample_id'];tic=row['tic'];d=json.loads((B/tic/'raw-fold.json').read_text());v,reason,nextcheck=NOTES[sid]
 psol=d['fold']['P'];p2=d['fold']['P2'];pwin=[w for w in d['windows'] if w['kind']=='P']
 cov='; '.join(f"s{w['sector']} {w['predicted_btjd']:.2f}: core {w['n_core']}, L/R {w['n_left']}/{w['n_right']}, {('%.1f ppt'%w['depth_ppt']) if w['depth_ppt'] is not None else 'unmeasurable'}" for w in pwin)
 sectors='; '.join(f"s{s['sector']} [{s['start']:.2f},{s['end']:.2f}], n={s['n']}, cadence={s['cadence']*1440:.1f} min" for s in d['sectors'])
 extra=(' The new sector cutout measurements and archive hashes are in [helper-newsectors.txt](helper-newsectors.txt), [wcs-placement.json](wcs-placement.json) and [helper-newsectors.png](helper-newsectors.png).' if sid=='H094' else ' The s86 reduction and pixel checks are in [helper-detail-086.png](helper-detail-086.png), [helper-pixel.txt](helper-pixel.txt) and [helper-pixel-difference.png](helper-pixel-difference.png); current s59/s85 coverage is in [followup-newsectors.json](followup-newsectors.json).' if sid=='H100' else '')
 occasion_note=('No binary period, primary epoch or depth is promoted from the insecure single event.' if sid=='H100' else 'No binary period, primary epoch or depth is promoted from these insecure occasions.' if v=='PLAUSIBLE' else 'This verdict refutes the selected repeating eclipse signal, not every possible binary configuration of the star.')
 body=f'''# {sid} — TIC {tic}\n\nPhysical verdict for the selected fold: **{v}**. Bounded review: **COMPLETE**. Catalogue novelty: **UNKNOWN**; central catalogue gates remain unavailable.\n\nGaia DR3 {row['gaia_dr3']} is an SB1 with spectroscopic period {float(row['gaia_period_days']):.5f} d. This is selection context, not a measured eclipse clock. The screening solution is P={psol['P']:.5f} d, duration {psol['dur']:.3f} d, z={psol['z']:.2f}, depth {psol['depth']:.0f} ppm; its P/2 test is {p2['P']:.5f} d, z={p2['z']:.2f}. Neither screening period is adopted as a photometric measurement.\n\n## Raw evidence and interpretation\n\n{reason}\n\nAll cached sectors were inspected in raw QLP SAP flux with QUALITY=0. Actual sector coverage (BTJD): {sectors}. The P-screened occasions, with observed core and separate left/right baseline counts, are: {cov}. These local medians are diagnostics, not fitted eclipse depths. Missing cadences and internal gaps are recorded in [raw-fold.json](raw-fold.json); [raw-fold.png](raw-fold.png) shows every full sector and both folds. P/2 windows and available KSPSAP measurements are in the numeric artifact.{extra} Predicted times are search windows, not measured event centers.\n\n## Limits and next check\n\n{nextcheck} {occasion_note} An alternate extraction of the same TESS photons tests processing, not recurrence.\n\n## Provenance\n\nThe frozen [source packet](../../source-packets/{tic}/sources.json) binds FITS paths, source hashes, Gaia metadata and original bulk/fold receipts. [SOURCE-HASHES.json](../SOURCE-HASHES.json) and [SHA256SUMS.json](../SHA256SUMS.json) seal the review artifacts.\n'''
 report=B/tic/'REPORT.md';report.write_text(body,encoding='utf-8')
 rows.append({'sample_id':sid,'tic':tic,'sample_stratum':row['sample_stratum'],'physical_verdict':v,'full_review_completion':'COMPLETE','novelty_status':'UNKNOWN','period_days':'','period_error_days':'','primary_epoch_btjd':'','depth_ppt':'','limitations':('Shallow two-occasion dips; timing aliases, source and pixel attribution unresolved.' if sid=='H094' else 'One isolated candidate dip; screened period contradicted by an observed null; source unverified.' if sid=='H100' else 'Selected fold rejected from raw trends/steps and observed contrary windows; unrelated variability not characterized.'),'next_check':nextcheck,'report':str(report)})
 pkt=B.parent/'source-packets'/tic/'sources.json';src=json.loads(pkt.read_text());hashes.append({'sample_id':sid,'tic':tic,'packet_path':str(pkt),'packet_sha256':hashlib.sha256(pkt.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'bulk_result':src['bulk_result'],'bulk_result_sha256':src['bulk_result_sha256'],'fold_result':src['fold_result'],'fold_result_sha256':src['fold_result_sha256'],'fits':[{'path':f['path'],'sha256':f['sha256']} for f in src['target']['files']]})
with (B/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=list(rows[0]));w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
(B/'SOURCE-HASHES.json').write_text(json.dumps(hashes,indent=2)+'\n')
print('wrote',len(rows),'reports')
